! **Ten sites, and a metal.** fcc aluminium as a `2 x 1 x 5` supercell of its
! one-atom primitive cell -- ten atoms, `marzari-vanderbilt` smearing, and the
! same pseudopotential and cutoff as `al2-metal.in` and `al4-metal.in`, so what
! this case adds over those is the size and the cell shape.
!
! It is the metal counterpart of `si10-nc.in`'s point about the symmetry search:
! stacking five cells along `a3` and two along `a1` puts coefficients of five in
! the rotation matrices, which a fixed `range(-3, 4)` window cannot represent.
! A metal is the more sensitive test of what that costs, because the Fermi
! level moves with the symmetrised density and every occupation moves with it.
!
! The 4x4x1 grid is the primitive 8x4x5 folded onto this cell.
 &control
    calculation = 'scf'
    tprnfor = .true.
    tstress = .true.
 /
 &system
    ibrav = 0, celldm(1) = 7.50, nat = 10, ntyp = 1,
    ecutwfc = 15.0,
    occupations = 'smearing', smearing = 'marzari-vanderbilt', degauss = 0.05
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
CELL_PARAMETERS alat
  -1.00  0.00  1.00
   0.00  0.50  0.50
  -2.50  2.50  0.00
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Al  26.98  Al.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Al    0.0000    0.0000    0.0000
 Al   -0.5000    0.5000    0.0000
 Al   -1.0000    1.0000    0.0000
 Al   -1.5000    1.5000    0.0000
 Al   -2.0000    2.0000    0.0000
 Al   -0.5000    0.0000    0.5000
 Al   -1.0000    0.5000    0.5000
 Al   -1.5000    1.0000    0.5000
 Al   -2.0000    1.5000    0.5000
 Al   -2.5000    2.0000    0.5000
K_POINTS automatic
 4 4 1 0 0 0
